            "payload" : {
              "isProxyPort" : false,
              "base" : {
                "portDescription" : "All 21 hand landmarks (MediaPipe's own HAND_CONNECTIONS order: 0=wrist, 1-4=thumb, 5-8=index, 9-12=middle, 13-16=ring, 17-20=little) as the model's metric, view-independent world shape, placed in Fabric's scene space so the default perspective camera sees it on top of the image: it keeps its metric size and only its position is fit to the image landmarks, so a hand that appears larger sits nearer the camera (larger z); a hand 1 m away sits on the image plane. A true 3D shape, so x\/y match the finger-group outputs only approximately. Directly comparable against MediaPipe Face\/Pose Landmarks' own 3D Landmarks output, so all three can be composited in one 3D scene — not physically metric, just a consistent shared space. Empty if nothing was detected.",
